# Relaxed CPU-speculation-mitigation posture for SINGLE-TENANT / first-party
# fleets, applied at build time via MITIGATIONS=relaxed.  Every mitigation stays
# COMPILED IN (see 50-security.x86_64 + the accept-defaults ledger) and is
# runtime-recoverable; this only bakes the boot-time default (mitigations=off)
# INTO THE IMAGE, so the posture is an attested property of the artifact rather
# than a deploy-time cmdline that can be forgotten or tampered.  The built-in
# line is appended to the bootloader's (x86 CMDLINE_OVERRIDE=n / arm64
# CMDLINE_EXTEND), so it wins as the later token but the bootloader can still
# add args.  DO NOT use on multi-tenant hosts -- tenant<->tenant microarch
# isolation is exactly what these mitigations provide.
CONFIG_CMDLINE="mitigations=off"
